          "message": "Failed checkpoint cleanup now suppresses retries for the full GC interval. StoreCheckpoints can exhaust the shared context before cleanup starts, yet lastCheckpointGC is advanced before cleanup runs. Listing or deletion failures likewise consume the interval despite unsuccessful cleanup.",
          "evidence": "RunOnce: `stepCtx, cancelFunc := context.WithDeadline(ctx, time.Now().Add(r.checkpointsWriteTimeout))`; `r.MaintainCheckpoints(stepCtx)`. MaintainCheckpoints: `r.checkpointWriter.StoreCheckpoints(ctx, r.updateWorkerCount)`; `r.lastCheckpointGC = time.Now()`; `r.clusterStateFeeder.GarbageCollectCheckpoints(ctx)`. GarbageCollectCheckpoints returns after listing errors and logs deletion errors without reporting failure to its caller. Previously, lastCheckpointGC advanced only when cleanup returned no error.",
